/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Dare to Speak, Connect, and Act"/><published>2026-07-05T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-07-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/speak-connect-act</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/speak-connect-act/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="discussion"/><category term="career"/><category term="systems thinking"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Silence is gold for how you treat people — but in the internet era, unspoken dreams disappear in the noise. Speak, connect, then act.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Confirm Demand Before You Build Anything</title><link href="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/demand-before-build/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Confirm Demand Before You Build Anything"/><published>2026-07-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-07-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/demand-before-build</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/demand-before-build/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="discussion"/><category term="career"/><category term="systems thinking"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Action without confirmed demand builds in the wrong direction — research the audience first, then align the product in a continuous loop.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">How to Start Your Business Model</title><link href="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/business-model-start/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="How to Start Your Business Model"/><published>2026-07-03T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-07-03T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/business-model-start</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/business-model-start/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="discussion"/><category term="career"/><category term="systems thinking"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The path from idea to scale is not build-first — it is demand discovery, paid MVP proof, then replication.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Academic Information Redundancy — The Next Research Frontier</title><link href="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/academic-research-frontier/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Academic Information Redundancy — The Next Research Frontier"/><published>2026-07-01T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-07-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/academic-research-frontier</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/academic-research-frontier/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="discussion"/><category term="AI"/><category term="academia"/><category term="urban science"/><category term="embodied AI"/><category term="research"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[In the AI era, academic research must move beyond information redundancy toward embodied observation, high-fidelity sensing, and Physical AI urban science.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Asymmetric Advantage in the AI Era</title><link href="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/ai-asymmetric-advantage/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Asymmetric Advantage in the AI Era"/><published>2026-06-25T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-25T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/ai-asymmetric-advantage</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sijie-yang.com/blog/2026/ai-asymmetric-advantage/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="discussion"/><category term="AI"/><category term="career"/><category term="society"/><category term="urban science"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[What truly matters in the AI era is not whether you can use AI, but whether you can reach information sources, decision centers, and resource allocation mechanisms.]]></summary></entry><entry><titl